## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design multi-input serving with optional inputs and multiple signatures in TF SavedModel.

## Key Concepts
- tf.saved_model, serving signatures, tf.keras.Input, tf.function, concrete functions, multiple signatures, default inputs.

## Code Example
```javascript
import tensorflow as tf

# Python-like example shown here for TF SavedModel export

def build_model():
    image = tf.keras.Input(shape=(224,224,3), name='image')
    feats = tf.keras.Input(shape=(10,), name='features')
    x = tf.keras.layers.Flatten()(image)
    x = tf.keras.layers.Concatenate()([x, feats])
    out = tf.keras.layers.Dense(1, activation='sigmoid')(x)
    return tf.keras.Model(inputs=[image, feats], outputs=out)

model = build_model()

@tf.function(input_signature=[tf.TensorSpec([None,224,224,3], tf.float32, name='image'),
                              tf.TensorSpec([None,10], tf.float32, name='features')])
def serve_full(image, features):
    return {'outputs': model([image, features])}

@tf.function(input_signature=[tf.TensorSpec([None,224,224,3], tf.float32, name='image')])
def serve_image_only(image):
    default_features = tf.zeros([tf.shape(image)[0], 10], dtype=tf.float32)
    return {'outputs': model([image, default_features])}

tf.saved_model.save(model, 'saved_model', signatures={
  'serving_default': serve_full.get_concrete_function(),
  'image_only': serve_image_only.get_concrete_function(),
})
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you version and test signature compatibility across model upgrades?
- How to monitor and fallback if image_only signature is called with missing features?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests multi-tenant inference design, signature layout, per-tenant batching, and observability in Kubernetes TF Serving.

## Key Concepts
- Shared backbone with per-tenant heads via multiple signatures
- Per-tenant batching configs and queues
- Isolation: separate queues, metrics, and cache boundaries
- Observability: per-tenant SLAs, latency percentiles, and QPS

## Code Example
```python
import tensorflow as tf
class Backbone(tf.keras.Model):
  def __init__(self):
    super().__init__(); self.layer = tf.keras.layers.Dense(64, activation='relu')
  def call(self, x): return self.layer(x)
class HeadA(tf.keras.Model):
  def __init__(self): super().__init__(); self.out = tf.keras.layers.Dense(2)
  def call(self, z): return self.out(z)
class HeadB(tf.keras.Model):
  def __init__(self): super().__init__(); self.out = tf.keras.layers.Dense(3)
  def call(self, z): return self.out(z)
class MultiTenant(tf.keras.Model):
  def __init__(self):
    super().__init__(); self.backbone = Backbone(); self.headA = HeadA(); self.headB = HeadB()
  @tf.function(input_signature=[tf.TensorSpec([None, 16], tf.float32)])
  def serve_headA(self, x):
    z = self.backbone(x)
    return {"logits": self.headA(z)}
  @tf.function(input_signature=[tf.TensorSpec([None, 16], tf.float32)])
  def serve_headB(self, x):
    z = self.backbone(x)
    return {"logits": self.headB(z)}
model = MultiTenant()
tf.saved_model.save(model, "saved/mt_serving", signatures={
  "serve_headA": model.serve_headA.get_concrete_function(),
  "serve_headB": model.serve_headB.get_concrete_function()
})
```

